{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For</b> — It is possible that the meaning of [the preceding phrase about] those who taunt me is: because they have taunted me, may HaShem send His kindness. And this is it: \"For [great] unto the heavens\" — and because the height of the heavens has a limit, but Your kindness has no limit, therefore after it: \"Be exalted above the heavens.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:06.421256329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}